# Monte Carlo evidence

Run `python3 analysis/monte_carlo.py` from the repository root. It writes `results/pi_mc.json`. Python, NumPy and SciPy versions are recorded in that file. An independent rerun can use `--output /path/to/rerun.json`; timing fields will differ.

The sample size is fixed by the objective, not selected from the results. Root seed 20261019 is chosen before execution. NumPy SeedSequence spawns 20 separate PCG64 streams; spawn keys identify the seeds reproducibly. No seeds are rejected or replaced. The first stream serves as a full-size timing pilot and is included; the remaining streams execute with two worker threads. Every generated pair counts toward the required 20,000,000 points.

The main interval is the two-sided Student t interval across 20 per-seed estimates, using sample SD with 19 degrees of freedom. Each estimate averages one million Bernoulli membership indicators, supporting the approximate normality needed by this interval. The interval describes repeated-simulation uncertainty, not uncertainty in the mathematical constant. The pooled-count mean is checked against the seed mean, and the empirical seed SD is compared with the theoretical binomial SD sqrt(pi*(4-pi)/1,000,000). These checks do not select results or change the prescribed interval.
